                        "entry_id": "d739eb08-5f4e-3081-a0ae-1394fdd9fbd1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prénom masculin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d74fb8fb-b195-46f2-92ae-fecc7e3000f6",
                                "sense_id": "3991f97e-0ed8-3176-9cb9-d88eee472576",
                                "text": "Herbert, Sydney, Milton, Seymour. You know, all the time I was growing up I thought those were the most ordinary Jewish first names, until someone pointed out that they were British last names. I guess to my great-grandparents those names must have sounded so modern, so sophisticated, so - non-Eastern European. And now they're just Uncle Miltie, Uncle Sy, Uncle Herb. Do other people have Uncle Donne and Uncle Wordsworth?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
